{
  "result": "The refrigerator hums at 2:13 AM and that is the only honest sound in my apartment. Everything else is performing.\n\nI have this theory that we have too many lights. Not light bulbs, but little lights. The dot on the TV. The charging indicator on my toothbrush. The green eye of the air purifier. They never sleep. They watch us trying to sleep and blink like they know something.\n\nYesterday I went to the hardware store just to walk down the aisle full of screws. There are hundreds of types of screws. Flat head, Phillips, Torx, hex, wood, machine, sheet metal. Someone, at some point, cared enough to invent a new kind of screw because the old one wasn't quite right. I find that incredibly moving.\n\nWe don't really fix things anymore, we replace them. But the screws remain. The idea of a screw remains - a simple piece of metal that holds two things together by turning.\n\nI think people are a lot like that. We get stripped, we rust, we don't quite fit the hole we were made for. But with a little pressure and rotation, we hold.\n\nI want to be a good screw. Not the flashiest one in the box. Just the one that doesn't come loose when it matters.\n\nAlso, I should probably defrost my freezer. It's been forming a small, very determined glacier in there since at least March, and I'm starting to respect its persistence. Maybe tomorrow. Probably not though. We'll see. Okay?",
